{
  "header": [
    "UNALLOCATED — a generic 500 carries `internal_error`; `io_error` and `storage_error` are used only",
    "for their own conditions. A MUST the specification itself says no wire client can drive.",
    "",
    "Batch 2. Reached by reading §3.3 whole (the 500 row and its satisfaction mode)."
  ],
  "id_status": "unallocated",
  "under": "",
  "title": "A 500 response carries `internal_error` unless `io_error` (OS I/O) or `storage_error` (store/tree) names the actual condition",
  "spec": "ENTITY-CORE-PROTOCOL §3.3 (500 row + default-code force)",
  "spec_also": [
    "§3.3 satisfaction mode ('500 — not drivable by a conformance client ... satisfied by a source audit')"
  ],
  "snapshot": "entity-core-protocol/v0.8.2.21",
  "level": "MUST",
  "profile": [
    "core"
  ],
  "surface": "unreachable",
  "status": "draft",
  "routed": "docs/status/FINDINGS-FROM-AUTHORING.md F16",
  "reading": [
    "§3.3's 500 row: \"Default `code` = `internal_error` — an internal step failed and no more-specific",
    "defined code applies (0.8.2.6). More-specific 500 codes where one applies (0.8.2.8): `io_error` ...",
    "`storage_error` ... The two are distinct conditions and are not interchangeable.\" Default-code force",
    "makes the default a MUST for the generic case, and makes an undefined spelling non-conformant.",
    "",
    "TWO CLAUSES, ONE SLOT. As with ECP-R44, the unit is the code slot at 500: {internal_error, io_error,",
    "storage_error}, each used for its own condition. \"Not interchangeable\" is part of what the slot",
    "means, not a second obligation.",
    "",
    "THE SPECIFICATION DECLARES IT UNREACHABLE, WHICH IS UNUSUAL AND WORTH TAKING AT ITS WORD. §3.3: \"500 —",
    "not drivable by a conformance client. A conformant peer cannot be made to fail internally on demand",
    "over the wire, so this row is satisfied by a SOURCE AUDIT of the implementation's emit sites at a",
    "named commit, not by a `validate-peer` check.\" And: \"a check MUST NOT be pinned to a row it cannot",
    "reach.\" That last sentence binds THIS REPO's suites. So there is no wire arm, no negative control,",
    "and the exclusion below names the class and the discharge.",
    "",
    "WHY AUTHOR A FILE AT ALL. Because the alternative is silence, and silence is indistinguishable from",
    "nobody having read the 500 row. The file makes the obligation countable and names what would",
    "discharge it.",
    "",
    "WHY `unallocated`. No §9 row names 500 codes. The discharge question (cross-peer observable? interop",
    "breaking?) is answered \"observable when it occurs, unforceable to make occur\" — which the CQ-9",
    "procedure does not have a branch for. F16."
  ],
  "preconditions": {
    "grants": [],
